# Mark binary files explicitly so core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default)
# doesn't strip CR bytes from inside them. The v3 poster PNG previously
# committed without this protection was silently corrupted (~7 KB of CRs
# stripped) — pdf-lib happened to tolerate the bad chunks, but the v4 swap
# made it visible: the committed blob was 37 KB smaller than the working
# tree. Don't trust autocrlf to leave binary content alone.

# Images
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.bmp binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary

# Vector / interchange formats that ARE text but we don't want EOL conversion
# disturbing (some tools embed binary payloads in SVG via base64).
*.svg binary

# Documents / archives
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.7z binary

# Audio / video
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.webm binary

# Fonts
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Anything compiled
*.wasm binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
